caption: Wraiths and the Shadow

In addition to the rest of the basic Wraith package, wraiths get a variation of Split Personality. Instead of a self control roll, the Wraith rolls a quick contest of Will between their real personality and their Shadow whenever an appropriately stressful situation arises. This explicitly includes any time a Wraith loses a point of Will. Shadows have an advantage in this sense: while a Wraith’s Will degrades with each oblivion roll failed, the Shadow’s will stays strong. Instead they gain derangements, mental disadvantages opposed to the morality of the Wraith’s main personality. They become degenerate, angry void-worshipping monsters. If the Shadow ever gains a Will that is 20 points stronger than the Wraith’s main personality, the Shadow can purge the Wraith forever, buying off the Split Personality and becoming the only personality. Such beings are no longer Wraiths; they are known as Banes, Demons, or Nephwracks depending on who is speaking. These creatures no longer degrade, but serve oblivion directly by tormenting and destroying Wraiths and killing humans when they can, seeking to pull more souls into oblivion.
